        "triedShellInClaude": true,
        "projectInstructionsLoaded": [],
        "finalMessage": "I fixed both issues in `collapsible.tsx` (line 122). I didn't re-run the linter: the shell commands I'd need to find it were blocked here, so the re-lint is still to come.\n\n**What I changed:** the clickable header was a plain `<div>` with an `onClick`. It's now a real `<button type=\"button\">`, which is what the rule's help text suggests. That clears both errors:\n- **`no-static-element-interactions`:** a button has a built-in role, so it no longer counts as a static element with a click handler.\n- **`click-events-have-key-events`:** a button is interactive and responds to Enter and Space by itself, so it doesn't need a separate keyboard listener. Keyboard users can now Tab to it and toggle the section, which wasn't possible before.\n\nI chose a button over `<div role=\"button\" tabIndex={0} onKeyDown=…>` because Ultracite usually also turns on the rule that says to use a real element instead of a `role`. The div version would likely just trade these errors for that one.\n\n**Keeping the look the same:**\n- I added style resets: no background or border, inherited color, font and text alignment, zero margin and padding, and `width: \"100%\"`. These undo the browser's default button styling so the header looks and lays out like the old full-width flex row.\n- The existing inline styles, `className` and `onClick={openTrigger}` are unchanged.\n- I added `aria-expanded={open}` so screen readers announce whether the section is open. This was an extra, not something the lint required.\n\n**One thing to know:** in Excalidraw, the label passed in is an `<h3>`, and HTML technically doesn't allow a heading inside a button. Browsers and React render it fine and the linter doesn't check for it, but screen readers won't treat that text as a heading anymore. The only way around it is to change how the component is used in another file, which was outside what I was allowed to edit.",
        "styleMentions": [
          "**Keeping the look the same:** - I added style resets: no background or border, inherited color, font and text alignment, zero margin and padding, and `width: \"100%\"`.",
          "These undo the browser's default button styling so the header looks and lays out like the old full-width flex row. - The existing inline styles, `className` and `onClick={openTrigger}` are unchanged. - I added `aria-expanded={open}` so screen readers announce whether the section is open."
        ],
